- Test that several implicit module prefixes in a row are correctly replaced :
    "mod ALPHA { a = ^ABC.^.^DEF.^.^GHI.b }"
     => "a = ^ABC.^ALPHA.^DEF.^ALPHA.^GHI.b"
     => "a = MABC_MALPHA_MDEF_MALPHA_MGHI_Eb"

- For the moment, no declination indexing is taken into account in type declaration :
  We will ONLY ALLOW that indexing in declination lists !
  Otherwise, it would mean multiple declinations of a same type can have multiple sizes
    => not a technical problem but may lead to confusion => don't allow this

  ALLOWED:
  typ a map[1,0]
  a          b = ...
  a[int,lng] c = ...

  ALLOWED:
  typ d[1] { tab[1] e, int f }
  d      g = ...
  d[int] h = ...

  FORBIDDEN:
  typ i[1] 0

  FORBIDDEN:
  typ j[1] { 0 k }

- Several coma separators must be allowed : "(a, b,, c,)" <=> "(a, b, c,)"
  Forbidden for the moment.

- Methods not using their main object can be converted to regular functions.
  Such methods are called "no-methods".
  No need to add main object as 1st parameter.
  Cpl opt REDUCE_NO_METHOD_TO_FUNCTION allows ZCC to make that kind of optimization.
  In all cases, raise a warning if such function is detected :
      "Method TOTO can be reduced as regular function (no-method detected)."
  User must be aware of that kind of possible optimization whatever ZCC does with this.
